                <pb facs="0829" n="735" xml:id="pg735"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr. Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2996.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my dispatch, No. 2988, of
                    the 21st instant, relative to Charles Barnet and William Leavitt, seamen
                    supposed to belong to the crew of the American schooner <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Competitor</hi> and who were captured on land, I now beg to inclose the
                    copies of the correspondence had with the Governor-General and the admiral of
                    the naval station regarding same.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O.
                    Williams.</hi></signed></closer>






